{"availability":"available","full":"stack-of-tasks/pinocchio","name":"pinocchio","description":"A fast and flexible implementation of Rigid Body Dynamics algorithms and their analytical derivatives","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":3791,"forks":588,"created":"2014-10-07T15:42:51Z","updated":"2026-10-13T07:29:17Z","license":"BSD-2-Clause","branch":"devel","homepage":"http://stack-of-tasks.github.io/pinocchio/","topics":["analytical-derivatives","automatic-differentiation","c-plus-plus","casadi","code-generation","conda","cppad","dynamics","fcl","kinematics","motion-planning","pinocchio","python","rigid-body-dynamics","robotics","ros","urdf"],"demo":"http://stack-of-tasks.github.io/pinocchio/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:20:56.722Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T08:20:56.722Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T08:20:56.722Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:55:05.782Z","stars":3780,"forks":581},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:48:31.753Z","stars":3784,"forks":582},{"at":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.640Z","stars":3786,"forks":584},{"at":"2026-10-16T08:20:56.722Z","stars":3791,"forks":588}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pinocchio is open-source software actively developed by the Willow team at Inria in the lovely city of Paris. Pinocchio instantiates state-of-the-art Rigid Body Algorithms for poly-articulated systems, building upon and revisiting the foundational algorithms introduced by Roy Featherstone.","Beyond traditional rigid-body dynamics formulations, Pinocchio delivers cutting-edge algorithmic solutions for modern robotics and physics-based simulation challenges. It efficiently handles closed-loop kinematic mechanisms, solves frictional contact problems, and differentiates physics computations — making it a powerful and versatile library for both research and industrial applications.","Pinocchio also provides analytical derivatives of the main Rigid Body Algorithms — such as the Recursive Newton-Euler Algorithm and the Articulated-Body Algorithm — enabling gradient-based optimization, control, and learning in both simulation and real-world settings."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stack-of-tasks/pinocchio/blob/devel/README.md","fingerprint":"6619d40fe2f8d4a3a359ec1a842d21baffff2562d205b51e3f620879af9c90be","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T22:55:05.856Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.719Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Pinocchio is open-source software actively developed by the Willow team at Inria in the lovely city of Paris. Pinocchio instantiates state-of-the-art Rigid Body Algorithms for poly-articulated systems, building upon and revisiting the foundational algorithms introduced by Roy Featherstone.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stack-of-tasks/pinocchio/blob/devel/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6619d40fe2f8d4a3a359ec1a842d21baffff2562d205b51e3f620879af9c90be","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stack-of-tasks/pinocchio/blob/devel/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.720Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T07:47:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stack-of-tasks/pinocchio/blob/devel/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T11:09:17.038Z","hash":"6619d40fe2f8d4a3a359ec1a842d21baffff2562d205b51e3f620879af9c90be","originalBytes":25997,"storedBytes":25997,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.640Z","subjects":[],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Developer tools","subjects":[],"evidence":[],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Animation & motion","Simulation & physics","Automation & workflows","Apple","Science"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"http://stack-of-tasks.github.io/pinocchio/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-16T08:40:19.787Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-16